.\"
.TH "mpvc-installer" "1" "September, 2026" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mpvc-installer - Automated deployment, updates, and configuration
manager for mpvc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
usage: mpvc-installer args # \[at]version v1.9 (c) gmt4 https://github.com/gmt4/mpvc
  check-update   : Check for updates
  check-reqs     : Check for required packages
  config         : Fetch mpv config
  config-user    : Fetch mpv config to BINDIR=/home/user/bin
  config-sys     : Fetch mpv config to BINDIR=/usr/local/bin
  fetch-user     : Fetch to BINDIR=/home/user/bin
  link-user      : Symlink to BINDIR=/home/user/bin
  install        : Install to BINDIR=/usr/local/bin
  uninstall      : Uninstall from BINDIR=/usr/local/bin
  install-user   : Install to BINDIR=/home/user/bin
  install-sys    : Install to BINDIR=/usr/local/bin (sets PREFIX=/usr/local)
  uninstall-user : Uninstall from BINDIR=/home/user/bin
  uninstall-sys  : Uninstall from BINDIR=/usr/local/bin (sets PREFIX=/usr/local)
*tips: If unsure where to start, start with: mpvc-installer fetch-user
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]mpvc-installer\f[R] is a dedicated deployment and configuration
manager for the \f[B]mpvc\f[R] ecosystem.
Written in POSIX-compliant shell scripting, it automates script
downloading, system-wide or user-level symlinking, dependency checks,
and default configuration setups.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
quickstart
Automated download, install, config, and setup.
Designed for first-time users under user home (\f[C]PREFIX=$HOME\f[R]).
.TP
quickstart-rm
Cleanup the installation performed by the quickstart routine.
.TP
check-update
Query the remote upstream Git repository to discover available software
updates.
.TP
check-reqs
Check the current mpvc installation, checking that required tools/deps
are present, and their versions (\f[C]mpv\f[R], \f[C]socat\f[R],
\f[C]gawk\f[R]).
.TP
config
Fetch the standard global baseline \f[C]mpv\f[R] communication
parameters and configuration targets.
.TP
config-user
Populate local user mpvc configuration directories under
\f[C]PREFIX=$HOME\f[R].
.TP
config-sys
Deploy default profiles globally for system-wide access under
\f[C]PREFIX=/usr/local\f[R].
.TP
fetch-user
Fetch the standalone script directly into the user home
(\f[C]PREFIX=$HOME\f[R]).
.TP
link-user
Create localized symlinks within \f[C]\[ti]/bin/\f[R] pointing to a
manually cloned repository tree.
.TP
install
Install the application binaries systematically to the system
\f[C]PREFIX=/usr/local/\f[R].
.TP
uninstall
Completely remove systemic application components from
\f[C]PREFIX=/usr/local/\f[R].
.TP
install-user
Install the application binaries systematically to the user home
\f[C]PREFIX=$HOME\f[R].
.TP
install-sys
Install the application binaries systematically to the system
\f[C]PREFIX=/usr/local/\f[R].
.TP
uninstall-user
Uninstall the application binaries systematically from user home
\f[C]PREFIX=$HOME\f[R].
.TP
uninstall-sys
Uninstall the application binaries systematically from the system
\f[C]PREFIX=/usr/local/\f[R].
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
PREFIX
Set the prefix pointing to the base installation directory.
Defaults to \f[C]/usr/local\f[R].
.TP
BINDIR
Explicitly overrides the destination binary folder path during localized
setups.
Defaults to \f[C]$PREFIX/bin\f[R].
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]\[ti]/.config/mpvc/\f[B]\f[R]
Destination directory where \f[C]config-user\f[R] stores the default
configurations for: \f[C]mpvc.conf\f[R], \f[C]mpv.conf\f[R], and
\f[C]yt-dlp.conf\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Perform a fully automated, standalone setup tracking standard user
folder limits:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mpvc-installer quickstart
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Completely purge and clean up environment trails introduced via the
quickstart interface:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mpvc-installer quickstart-rm
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Audit your current install for required tools/versions (such as socat or
gawk):
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mpvc-installer check-reqs
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Extract and mirror the default configuration profile layout assets
inside your user profile directory path:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mpvc-installer config-user
\f[R]
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
